1. Introduction
  - A well-designed Layer 2 network will have redundant switches and paths to ensure that if one switch goes down, another path to a different switch is available to forward data. 
  - Users of the network would not experience any disruption of service. 
  - Redundancy in a hierarchical network design fixes the problem of a single point of failure, yet it can create a different kind of problem called Layer 2 loops.
  - A Layer 2 loop can happen very quickly and make it impossible to use the network. 
  - There are a few common ways that a Layer 2 loop can be created and propagated. 
  - Spanning Tree Protocol (STP) is designed specifically to eliminate Layer 2 loops in your network.

